#: ../../../Telemetry.md:1
msgid "Telemetry framework in LLVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:7
msgid "Objective"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:9
msgid ""
"Provides a common framework in LLVM for collecting various usage and "
"performance metrics. It is located at `llvm/Telemetry/Telemetry.h`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:13
msgid "Characteristics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:15
msgid "Configurable and extensible by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:17
msgid ""
"Tools: any tool that wants to use Telemetry can extend and customize it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:18
msgid ""
"Vendors: Toolchain vendors can also provide custom implementation of the "
"library, which could either override or extend the given tool's upstream "
"implementation, to best fit their organization's usage and privacy models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:21
msgid ""
"End users of such tool can also configure Telemetry (as allowed by their "
"vendor)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:24
msgid "Important notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:26
msgid ""
"There is no concrete implementation of a Telemetry library in upstream LLVM. "
"We only provide the abstract API here. Any tool that wants telemetry will "
"implement one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:30
msgid ""
"The rationale for this is that all the tools in LLVM are very different in "
"what they care about (what/where/when to instrument data). Hence, it might "
"not be practical to have a single implementation. However, in the future, if "
"we see enough common pattern, we can extract them into a shared place. This "
"is TBD - contributions are welcome."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:36
msgid ""
"No implementation of Telemetry in upstream LLVM shall store any of the "
"collected data due to privacy and security reasons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:39
msgid "Different organizations have different privacy models:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:41
msgid "Which data is sensitive, which is not?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:42
msgid ""
"Whether it is acceptable for instrumented data to be stored anywhere? (to a "
"local file, what not?)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:45
msgid ""
"Data ownership and data collection consents are hard to accommodate from "
"LLVM developers' point of view:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:48
msgid ""
"E.g., data collected by Telemetry is not necessarily owned by the user of an "
"LLVM tool with Telemetry enabled, hence the user's consent to data "
"collection is not meaningful. On the other hand, LLVM developers have no "
"reasonable ways to request consent from the \"real\" owners."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:53
msgid "High-level design"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:55
msgid "Key components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:57
msgid "The framework consists of four important classes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:59
msgid ""
"`llvm::telemetry::Manager`: The class responsible for collecting and "
"transmitting telemetry data. This is the main point of interaction between "
"the framework and any tool that wants to enable telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:62
msgid "`llvm::telemetry::TelemetryInfo`: Data courier"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:63
msgid ""
"`llvm::telemetry::Destination`: Data sink to which the Telemetry framework "
"sends data. Its implementation is transparent to the framework. It is up to "
"the vendor to decide which pieces of data to forward and where to forward "
"them to for their final storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:68
msgid "`llvm::telemetry::Config`: Configurations for the `Manager`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:73
msgid "How to implement and interact with the API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:75
msgid ""
"To use Telemetry in your tool, you need to provide a concrete implementation "
"of the `Manager` class and `Destination`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Telemetry.md:77
msgid ""
"Define a custom `Serializer`, `Manager`, `Destination` and optionally a "
"subclass of `TelemetryInfo`"
msgstr ""

